id: ops-hkxb
title: Prevent symlink cycles during docstring source traversal
description: collectSourceFiles follows directory symlinks through statSync without remembering canonical paths. A directory link back to an ancestor can recurse until stack exhaustion instead of returning a controlled fail-closed result.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T10:31:08.883Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T10:32:43.196Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-31T10:32:43.165Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-31T10:32:43.165Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: Traversal keys visited directories by real path; Canonicalization failures produce a controlled fail-closed error; A real symlink-cycle regression completes and preserves source coverage
parent: ops-073p
reporter: coderabbitai
severity: medium
environment: PR 33 exact head b610690
repro_steps: "Place a directory symlink beneath the scan root that resolves to the root itself, then run analyzeDocstringCoverage."
resolution: Each directory is canonicalized through realpathSync under a contextual fail-closed error boundary and traversed only once through a visited set.
expected_result: Each canonical directory is traversed at most once; cycles terminate deterministically while source files remain covered.
actual_result: "A real directory symlink back to the scan root completes deterministically, scans the authored TypeScript file exactly once, checks its declaration, and reports no false violation."
component: docstring-traversal
regression: true
customer_impact: A repository symlink cycle can crash the fleet gate with an uncontrolled stack overflow.
files[1]{path,scope,note}:
  docstrings.ts,project,Canonical traversal guard
tests[1]{command,path,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  node --test --test-name-pattern='symlink cycle' test/docstrings.test.ts,test/docstrings.test.ts,project,60
close_reason: Canonical-path traversal guard prevents directory symlink recursion while preserving coverage.
body: ""
